# Story 39: Help & History (40s)
# Hook: Forget a command? Rysh tells you. ##help lists everything, ##history recalls what you typed.
# Duration: 40s
# Source: story-039-help-and-history.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 7

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Forget a command? Rysh tells you. ##help lists everything, ##history recalls what you typed.

[00:03.0 --> 00:07.0]
Launch rysh and run a couple of shell commands to build up some history.

[00:07.0 --> 00:14.0]
Every command you run is remembered, per input mode.

[00:14.0 --> 00:20.0]
Double-press Escape twice to reach rysh mode -- the prompt becomes a double-hash, ready for system commands.

[00:20.0 --> 00:28.0]
Type ##help to list every system command Rysh understands -- tabs, panes, lanes, sharing, snapshots, and more.

[00:28.0 --> 00:37.0]
Type ##history -- or just ##h -- to see the command history for the current input mode. Nothing gets lost.

[00:37.0 --> 00:40.0]
Help and history: your two-command safety net inside any pane.

